From: Nmap Upstream
Subject: Guard close_nse() when NOLUA is enabled

When Nmap is configured with --without-liblua, NOLUA is defined and
nse_main.h is not included. In that configuration, close_nse() is not
declared, which causes nmap.cc to fail to compile.

Wrap close_nse() with #ifndef NOLUA to match the other NSE callsites.

diff --git a/nmap.cc b/nmap.cc
index 33f5245..7e8e6f8 100644
--- a/nmap.cc
+++ b/nmap.cc
@@ -1858,6 +1858,8 @@ void nmap_free_mem() {
   AllProbes::service_scan_free();
   traceroute_hop_cache_clear();
   nsock_set_default_engine(NULL);
+#ifndef NOLUA
   close_nse();
+#endif
 }
 
 int nmap_main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
